# Theme Architecture Rules

Read `AGENTS.md` before generating or editing code in this theme.

Core rules:

- This is the Sanity CMS edition of an Astro and Tailwind CSS theme. Content lives in Sanity and is edited in Sanity Studio.
- Reuse existing components, widgets, cards, schemas, queries, styles, and patterns.
- Studio schemas live in `sanity/schemaTypes/` (`documents/`, `singletons/`, `sections/`, `objects/`), registered in `sanity/schemaTypes/index.ts`.
- The website data layer lives in `src/lib/sanity/`: GROQ in `queries.ts`, typed getters in `data.ts`, types in `types.ts`. Components use the getters, never the client directly.
- Section components live in `src/layouts/components/sections/` and are mapped by `_type` in `PageSections.astro`.
- For every new section: schema + registration in `index.ts` and `objects/pageSections.ts`, projection in `sectionsFields`, type in `types.ts`, component with `content` and `dataSanity` props, mapping in `PageSections.astro`, and demo data in `scripts/sanity/build-seed.mjs` (regenerate `sanity/seed/demo-content.json`).
- Put editable copy, links, images, buttons, and options in Sanity fields with beginner-friendly titles and descriptions. Do not hardcode content in components.
- Without a project ID the site runs the same queries against the demo seed, so keep the seed valid.
- `stegaClean` non-text values (enums, URLs, slugs, languages, form field names, SEO/meta) in `data.ts`; never derive ids or classes from possibly encoded strings.
- Never use `SANITY_API_READ_TOKEN` in client code or commit `.env`.
- Use `CustomButton.astro`, `Icons.astro`, `SanityImage.astro`, and `OptimizedImage.astro` instead of rebuilding shared primitives.
- Use nearest Tailwind theme values from `src/styles/theme.css`.
- Avoid Tailwind arbitrary values.
- Check `base.css`, `components.css`, and `safe.css` before adding new CSS or duplicated utility classes.
- Do not add heading classes already covered by `base.css`, including default font weight, tracking, leading, or wrapping classes.
- Keep imports clean. Do not add unused wrappers, unused JS, or duplicate abstractions.
- Prefer static rendering. Add client JavaScript only for required interaction.
- Keep copy generic for a shippable theme; avoid hardcoded brand names in reusable content, schema descriptions, and seed data.

Before finishing:

- Run `npm run astro-check` after code or schema changes.
- Run `SANITY_STUDIO_PROJECT_ID=<any-id> npx sanity schema validate` after Studio schema changes.
- Run `npm run build` for broad changes that affect routing, the data layer, the seed, or assets.
